---
import BaseLayout from '../../components/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumb from '../../components/Breadcrumb.astro';
import ShareBar from '../../components/ShareBar.astro';

const title = "Passport Size Photo Specifications Guide (2026)";
const description = "Everything you need to know about official passport photo dimensions, background requirements, and file size limits for exams.";

const howToSchema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "HowTo",
  "name": "How to Create a Passport Photo",
  "description": "Step-by-step guide on creating a compliant passport photo for online forms.",
  "step": [
    { "@type": "HowToStep", "name": "Prepare your photo", "text": "Take a clear front-facing photo with a plain background." },
    { "@type": "HowToStep", "name": "Open the Passport Photo Maker", "text": "Navigate to the FormFix Passport Photo Maker." },
    { "@type": "HowToStep", "name": "Upload and crop", "text": "Upload your photo and adjust the crop to 3.5cm x 4.5cm." },
    { "@type": "HowToStep", "name": "Download", "text": "Download your compliant passport photo." }
  ]
};
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} active="tools" canonicalPath="/guides/passport-photo-specifications" customSchema={howToSchema} ogType="article" publishedTime="2026-01-25" modifiedTime="2026-07-17">
    <Breadcrumb items={[{ name: 'Home', path: '/' }, { name: "Passport Size Photo Specifications Guide", path: "/guides/passport-photo-specifications" }]} />

    <section class="page-header">
        <div class="container">
            <h1>Passport Photo Specifications</h1>
            <p class="subtitle">Official requirements for UPSC, SSC, and Passport applications.</p>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section">
        <div class="container container-narrow">
            <article class="prose">
                <p>Ensuring your passport-size photo meets official standards is the most important step in any government application. Small errors in dimensions, background color, or file size often lead to immediate rejection, costing you time and effort. This comprehensive guide outlines the current specifications for major examination portals and explains how to capture the perfect shot from home.</p>
                
                <h2>Common Dimensions Across Portals</h2>
                <p>Different organizations have slightly different requirements, but most competitive exams in India (UPSC, SSC, Banking) follow a standard set of rules:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>Standard Dimensions:</strong> 3.5 cm width by 4.5 cm height.</li>
                    <li><strong>Face Coverage:</strong> The face should typically occupy 70% to 80% of the total frame area.</li>
                    <li><strong>Pixel Resolution:</strong> Usually 413 x 531 pixels for high-quality printing.</li>
                </ul>
                <p>For international requirements, such as a US Visa application, the standard changes to a 2 inch x 2 inch (51 mm x 51 mm) square format with strict rules on eye level placement.</p>

                <h2>Lighting and Background Requirements</h2>
                <p>Portals use automated software to verify photos, which means clarity is essential:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>Background:</strong> A plain white or very light off-white background is almost universally required. Avoid shadows on the wall or on your face.</li>
                    <li><strong>Clothing:</strong> Wear dark-colored clothes that provide a clear contrast against a white background. Avoid uniforms or clothing that matches the background color.</li>
                    <li><strong>Expression:</strong> Maintain a neutral facial expression with both eyes open and looking directly at the camera. Smiling is generally discouraged for official identification.</li>
                </ul>

                <h2>The File Size Challenge: The 20KB-50KB Bracket</h2>
                <p>This is where most applicants struggle. Portals like the UPSC Online application often require images to be strictly within a <strong>20KB to 50KB</strong> window. If your photo is 19.5KB, it will be rejected; if it is 50.1KB, it will be rejected. This requires a tool with mathematical precision to hit the target without making the face blurry.</p>

                <h2>Capturing your Photo at Home</h2>
                <p>You don't need a professional studio to get a valid photo. Follow these steps using your smartphone:</p>
                <ol>
                    <li><strong>Find natural light:</strong> Stand facing a window during the day for soft, even lighting on your face.</li>
                    <li><strong>Use a plain wall:</strong> Stand about 2 feet away from a white wall to minimize shadows.</li>
                    <li><strong>Level the camera:</strong> Have someone else take the photo with the camera at your eye level. Avoid selfies as they can distort facial features.</li>
                </ol>

                <h2>How FormFix Streamlines the Process</h2>
                <p>Our <a href="/passport-size-photo">Passport Photo Maker</a> is engineered to handle these specific rules automatically. When you upload your raw photo:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li>The system helps you crop specifically for the 3.5×4.5cm ratio.</li>
                    <li>Our AI-assisted background removal tool can help clean up minor wall imperfections.</li>
                    <li>The integrated compressor allows you to target exactly 20KB or 50KB with a single click, ensuring your file is accepted on the first attempt.</li>
                </ul>

                <div class="cta-box mt-32">
                    <h3>Get Your Photo Ready Today</h3>
                    <p>Save time and avoid rejection by using our specialized official photo maker.</p>
                    <a href="/passport-size-photo" class="primary-btn">Create Your Passport Photo</a>
                </div>
            </article>
        </div>
    </section>

    <ShareBar title={title} />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
    .page-header { padding: 80px 0 40px; background: var(--surface-2); text-align: center; }
    .content-section { padding: 60px 0; }
    .prose { line-height: 1.8; color: var(--text-secondary); }
    .container-narrow { max-width: 800px; }
    .cta-box { background: var(--accent-soft); padding: 32px; border-radius: 16px; text-align: center; }

    @media (max-width: 640px) {
        .page-header { padding: 40px 0; }
        .page-header h1 { font-size: 1.5rem; }
    }
</style>
